cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AKT Reader — Evidence Lab"
message: "If you use AKT Reader, please cite this software and the specific release or commit SHA."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Goldstein
    given-names: Jacob
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-04"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/jakegold1647/aktreader-research"
url: "https://github.com/jakegold1647/aktreader-research"
abstract: >-
  Evidence, methodology, and reproducibility tooling for local,
  uncertainty-aware extraction from historical civil-register acts in Russian
  Cyrillic and Polish. The evidence lab publishes the schemas, the
  evaluation-only gold corpus, the blind dual-reader consensus and
  adjudication method, and the measured local baseline. It makes no validated
  handwriting-accuracy claim; the single measured baseline is recorded as a
  weak research-derived before-picture.
keywords:
  - historical records
  - handwritten text recognition
  - Cyrillic
  - genealogy
  - provenance
  - uncertainty
  - research software
